Calc: threaded formula group calculation builds the document's default cell format before the worker threads start.

The worker threads of a threaded group calculation read cell number formats (VLOOKUP keys, cell values). A
column without any formatted cell answers with the document's default cell format, which
ScDocument::getCellAttributeHelper() and CellAttributeHelper::getDefaultCellAttribute() create on first use
without any lock. A document whose cells were all set without a format (import through ScDocumentImport, API)
reaches its first threaded calculation without them, so every worker thread tried to create them at once; one
thread replaced the helper the others were using, which then read freed memory: crashes in
SfxItemPool::GetUserOrPoolDefaultItem <- ScPatternAttr::GetNumberFormat, in ScDocument::getCellAttributeHelper
and in ~ScQueryEntry, from ScInterpreter::CalculateLookup in ScColumn::CalculateInThread. The main thread now
builds both before it starts the threads (one call next to the existing non-threaded formatter set-up).

License: modified upstream file keeps its license (MPL-2.0).
Test: CppunitTest_sc_ucalc_sharedformula testSharedFormulaWholeColumnShiftEndListening (20 000 grouped VLOOKUPs
filled through ScDocumentImport, then CalcAll: the threaded calculation crashed before this change).
---
--- a/sc/source/core/data/formulacell.cxx
+++ b/sc/source/core/data/formulacell.cxx
@@ -41,6 +41,7 @@
 #include <rangenam.hxx>
 #include <rangelst.hxx>
 #include <dbdata.hxx>
+#include <patattr.hxx>
 #include <progress.hxx>
 #include <scmatrix.hxx>
 #include <rechead.hxx>
@@ -5201,6 +5202,9 @@
         };
 
         SvNumberFormatter* pNonThreadedFormatter = rDocument.GetNonThreadedContext().GetFormatTable();
+        // HST Office: the worker threads read cell formats, and a document whose cells were all set without
+        // a format (import, API) has not built its default cell format yet: build it here, not in the threads.
+        rDocument.getCellAttributeHelper().getDefaultCellAttribute();
 
         comphelper::ThreadPool& rThreadPool(comphelper::ThreadPool::getSharedOptimalPool());
         sal_Int32 nThreadCount = rThreadPool.getWorkerCount();
